  "optionExplanations": {
    "A": "This would cause right pleural air with shift to the left, not the stated pattern.",
    "B": "Correct: left pleural air with pressure effect shifts the mediastinum to the right.",
    "C": "A pleural effusion produces fluid opacity rather than free pleural air and mediastinal shift from tension air is more likely here.",
    "D": "Pneumomediastinum is air in the mediastinum rather than a unilateral pleural air collection with shift.",
    "E": "Bilateral pneumothoraces may occur, but the classic tension pattern described is unilateral with mediastinal shift."
  },
